+/// Hasher for the glyph-cache shard maps. The derived `Hash` of
+/// [`GlyphCacheKey`] makes 12 small `write_*` calls per key and the map is
+/// probed once per glyph occurrence, so std's SipHash-1-3 dominated the probe.
+/// foldhash's `fast::RandomState` is still seeded (per-process global seed plus
+/// a per-map seed), which keeps attacker-chosen keys (font bytes, glyph ids,
+/// matrices all come from the PDF) from being pre-computed into collisions.
+type GlyphHashState = foldhash::fast::RandomState;
+
 #[derive(Debug, Default)]
